{"ref":"BDB, מוּצָק⁴","hw":"מוּצָק⁴","html":"† II. <big><span dir=\"rtl\">מוּצָק</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">מוּצַק</span></big>  <strong>n.</strong>[<strong>m.</strong>] <strong>constraint, distress</strong>;—abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">מוּצָק</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 8:23\" href=\"/Isaiah.8.23\">Is 8:23</a> <em>distress;</em> abs. also <span dir=\"rtl\">מוּצַק</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 36:16\" href=\"/Job.36.16\">Jb 36:16</a>, of distress as <em>constraint</em> (opp. <span dir=\"rtl\">רַחַב</span>); <span dir=\"rtl\">רֹחַב מַיִם בְּמוּצָ֑ק</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 37:10\" href=\"/Job.37.10\">37:10</a>, lit. <em>in constraint</em> (i.e. forzen).—i. <span dir=\"rtl\">מוּצָק</span> v. <a data-ref=\"BDB, יָצַק\" href=\"/BDB,_יָצַק\", dir=\"rtl\">יצק</a>.","next":"BDB, מָצוֹק²","prev":"BDB, צוּקָה"}